Summary:
---------

Regex is a powerful way to search, validate, extract, and replace text.
Python provides regex support through the re module.
Frequently used functions:
re.search() → Find the first match
re.match() → Match from the beginning of the string
re.findall() → Return all matches
re.sub() → Replace matches
re.split() → Split text using a pattern

If you're just starting out, focus on learning these core regex elements:

\d (digits)
\w (word characters)
\s (whitespace)
. (any character)
*, +, ? (quantifiers)
[] (character classes)
^ and $ (start/end anchors)